PS4HEN — Custom Notice
======================

Original Work
-------------
This project is based on "afterglow" by well0nez and m0zz.
All original exploit code, kernel patch logic, and core runtime files
(afterglow.js, jb.js, jb.html, core.js, mem.js, int64.js, ps4_offsets.js,
launch.js, style.css, cache.appcache) are the work of well0nez/m0zz and are
reproduced here under the terms of the GNU Affero General Public License v3
(AGPL-3.0), as originally published. A copy of that license is available at:

    https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt

Third-Party Components
----------------------
The following bundled files are not covered by this notice and retain their
own respective licenses:

  goldhen.bin          — GoldHEN, included with permission of SiSTRo
  patchset-1400.bin    — kernel patch set for firmware 14.00
  patchset-1352.bin    — kernel patch set for firmware 13.52

Modifications
-------------
The following changes were made by jw-notes (2026):

  - Removed the ps4-hen payload option; GoldHEN is now the only payload
  - Renamed the UI from "afterglow" to "PS4HEN"
  - Replaced the meme image with the GoldHEN logo (goldhen.png)
  - Moved the logo above the launch form and into the top bar
  - Updated the byline to credit original authors and note modifications
  - Added a PS4 browser user-agent check that blocks the start button
    on non-PS4 browsers with a clear error message
  - Refreshed the visual design: dark gold theme for the GoldHEN card,
    improved button styling, updated color tokens in style.css
  - Added favicon (goldhen.png) to both index.html and jb.html
  - Replaced the AGPL-3.0 LICENSE file with this custom notice

